# ============================================================
# RAGgamuffin privacy model:
#   - The PIPELINE (prompts, docs, config) is committed.
#   - The KNOWLEDGE (vault note contents) is NOT committed.
#
# Committed vault directories (pipeline structure, not knowledge):
#   vault/samples/    — sample notes for smoke-testing the pipeline
#   vault/_views/     — Obsidian Bases templates (.base files) and overview note
#   vault/03_meta/backlog.md
#   vault/03_meta/sentinel-state.template.md
# ============================================================

# Vault note contents stay local (privacy: may contain company code/notes).
# Folder structure is preserved via .gitkeep files.
vault/01_unprocessed/*
!vault/01_unprocessed/.gitkeep
vault/02_wiki/*
!vault/02_wiki/.gitkeep
vault/03_meta/archive/*
!vault/03_meta/archive/.gitkeep
vault/03_meta/changelogs/*
!vault/03_meta/changelogs/.gitkeep

# 03_meta: only the committed backlog template is tracked; everything else
# (generated logs, scratch files) stays local.
vault/03_meta/*
!vault/03_meta/backlog.md
!vault/03_meta/sentinel-state.template.md

# Obsidian machine-specific state (workspace layout, cache, plugin data).
# If you ever want to sync Obsidian *settings* across machines, selectively
# un-ignore .obsidian/app.json etc. — never workspace.json.
.obsidian/
vault/.obsidian/

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Msty Claw local artifacts (if it ever writes state into the workspace)
.claw/
*.log
